# Commit messages

Match existing git history. Prefer this over Conventional Commits (`feat:` / `fix:`) or untagged subjects.

## Format

```text
[Category] Short summary
```

- One-line subject; **no commit body** unless detail is truly necessary.
- Sentence case after the tag; concise phrase (roughly 30–60 characters typical).
- Describe the change clearly; avoid filler like `tmp commit` or untagged subjects.

## Categories

| Tag | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `[Feature]` | New capability or user-visible milestone |
| `[Fix]` | Bugfix |
| `[Refactor]` | Internal restructure without a new product feature |
| `[Cleanup]` | Deps, accuracy tidy-ups, small display/docs/process hygiene |
| `[Documentation]` | Doc-only changes (optional; `[Cleanup]` is also used for docs) |

## Examples

```text
[Feature] Retrieve model data from the back-end, display in table
[Refactor] Restructure filters layout and code organization
[Cleanup] Bring docs up to higher accuracy
[Fix] Fix Python/JS date conversion issues
```

## Also required

Every commit must update `docs/status.md` (see `.cursor/rules/status.mdc`).
